# Claude Code profiles: two accounts, one shared configuration

Two profiles, two Anthropic accounts, two quotas. **busirocket** (personal, the
default) is plain `claude`; **favish** is `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR="$HOME/.claude-favish"
claude` - write `$HOME`, never a bare `~`, because an unexpanded tilde makes
Claude Code create `./~/.claude-favish/` under the current directory, which is
how a `~` directory appeared in `~/p` on 2026-09-04. Everything but credentials
and session state is shared by symlink; the full map is in
`claude-profile-safety`.

**Never set `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=~/.claude`.** Unset, Claude Code reads `$HOME/.claude.json`;
set, it reads `$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/.claude.json`, so pointing it at `~/.claude`
starts a THIRD, empty profile with its own login and none of the MCP servers.
It fails silently — servers simply do not appear.

Two more: editing a file
under `~/.claude-favish/` directly is a bug (it belongs in `~/.claude` and
should be linked, or it is session state); and **a missing MCP server reads as a
broken browser**, so compare the two profiles' server lists before debugging
Chrome.

Invoke `claude-profile-safety` before starting a session under another account,
before editing or linking shared global configuration, and when tools or an
identity are missing for reasons that are not obvious.
